{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "03O6", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-fpqc-descent}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:188b1879ad8159744860f49feefa46c9e5ae006d639daafa08cba791d74aad2c", "source_text": "Faithfully flat descent", "source_text_hash": "sha256:11454d5b0d821b8de2c91be229a4e0937a58d784fef621b4aa35e9807957d9fb", "unit_id": "tag:03O6:title"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03O6", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:62118c6edf43c715ad6dc7e2fa3311bf06eac59580fbb6dfb0692421ec440861", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we discuss faithfully flat descent for quasi-coherent\nmodules. More precisely, we will prove quasi-coherent modules satisfy\neffective descent with respect to fpqc coverings.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:89e6adea486cb7f46adae220da20fb4098fb6a28b2b5cba53fec5605ddf7ae96", "unit_id": "tag:03O6:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03O6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{ t_i : T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0003": "$((\\mathcal{F}_i)_{i \\in I}, (\\varphi_{ij})_{i, j \\in I})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}_i$", "MATH_0005": "$T_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\varphi_{ij} : \\text{pr}_0^* \\mathcal{F}_i \\to\n\\text{pr}_1^* \\mathcal{F}_j$", "MATH_0007": "$T_i \\times_T T_j$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\text{pr}_0^*\\mathcal{F}_i \\ar[dr]_{\\text{pr}_{02}^*\\varphi_{ik}}\n\\ar[rr]^{\\text{pr}_{01}^*\\varphi_{ij}} & &\n\\text{pr}_1^*\\mathcal{F}_j \\ar[dl]^{\\text{pr}_{12}^*\\varphi_{jk}} \\\\\n& \\text{pr}_2^*\\mathcal{F}_k\n}\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$T_i \\times_T T_j \\times_T T_k$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0011": "$T$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{O}_{T_i}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\varphi_i : t_i^* \\mathcal{F} \\cong \\mathcal{F}_i$", "MATH_0014": "$\\varphi_{ij}$", "MATH_0015": "$$\n\\varphi_{ij} = \\text{pr}_1^* (\\varphi_j) \\circ \\text{pr}_0^* (\\varphi_i)^{-1}.\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-descent-datum}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6dfd224e622d937fed0b59c1bdff669fd09b9df7033929c901736b2d08c975fe", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:09d9c2022b99e9dd08ccd5eba2454bb64b6a0db22033732772a587c523fd35d5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a family of\nmorphisms of schemes with fixed target. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>descent datum<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> for\nquasi-coherent sheaves with respect to <MATH_0002> is a collection\n<MATH_0003> where\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is a quasi-coherent sheaf on <MATH_0005>, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0006> is an isomorphism of modules\non <MATH_0007>,\n<STRUCT_0004>\nsuch that the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>cocycle condition<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> holds: the diagrams\n<MATH_0008>\ncommute on <MATH_0009>.\nThis descent datum is called <TEXTITOPEN_0003>effective<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> if there exist a quasi-coherent\nsheaf <MATH_0010> over <MATH_0011> and <MATH_0012>-module isomorphisms\n<MATH_0013> compatible with\nthe maps <MATH_0014>, namely\n<MATH_0015>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0e55edf0f409dbef0f7d66111e294393a2c7cbd93d8640fd8afd653b9b9f1bae", "unit_id": "tag:03O7:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03O6", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:62118c6edf43c715ad6dc7e2fa3311bf06eac59580fbb6dfb0692421ec440861", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this and the next section we discuss some ingredients of the proof\nof the following theorem, as well as some related material.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aa9e7917f0e848d8116acda3e0113a368140694a2eee7087f8faa243ec72cc0f", "unit_id": "tag:03O6:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "03O6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{V} = \\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{V}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-descent-quasi-coherent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f7c14471f7c76dfa12251e329e2bf0b3f9d3fcc38a2cb6fd1b5e56792f20bb13", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:47198d2d451235af763f5d85ff7f05cae07cb4bb726a79959b1a8df9d3559006", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is an fpqc covering, then all\ndescent data for quasi-coherent sheaves with respect to <MATH_0002>\nare effective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4cc977a53e93c8608a70f428e556e40b8506d1343a93d84f59309e6591032479", "unit_id": "tag:03O8:statement"}
